    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=2x+1$, where $x\\ne-1$.\n\nSubtract $2x$ from $y$; since $x+1=\\dfrac{2}{1-t}\\ne0$, $x=-1$ is excluded.",
      "worked": "The parameter satisfies $t\\ne1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-2x&=\\frac{3+t}{1-t}-\\frac{2(1+t)}{1-t}\\\\y-2x&=\\frac{1-t}{1-t}\\\\y-2x&=1.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAlso,\n\n$$x+1=\\frac{2}{1-t}\\ne0.$$\n\nThus $y=2x+1$, where $x\\ne-1$. Conversely, every $x\\ne-1$ gives $t=\\dfrac{x-1}{x+1}\\ne1$, so there are no further restrictions.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
